 ## KVMem historical GC in the integrated server
 
+`--kvmem-checkpoint-mib N` sets the aggregate checkpoint budget C for one Program
+(positive MiB; default 1024 whenever KVMem is enabled). It is separate from Host
+KV payload H, source S, source-preparation R and GC auxiliary M. C charges pinned
+images (including idle pool buffers and execution leases), checkpoint metadata
+capacities and construction/rollback reservations. Removing a directory entry
+does not refund an object still held by another owner. The optional spread policy's
+`KVMEM_CHECKPOINT_HOST_MIB` remains an additional cap, never permission to exceed C.
+For disk history, C reserves its one existing read-staging buffer before images
+are admitted. C is an account of these owners/reservations, not a process RSS cap.
+
+Required captures first trim idle buffers and reclaim eligible older cache
+domains, protecting the admitted restore source. If the required state still
+does not fit, the request ends with an explicit unavailable quota error; optional
+captures may be skipped. Raising C can retain more reuse opportunities. `/stats`
+reports the effective budget, image/metadata/idle charges, peak, denied operations
+and separate actual/reserved read-staging bytes.
+
 The KVMem integration in `ninfer-serve` provides `--kvmem-gc-lru` and
 `--kvmem-gc-redundancy` (the latter requires `--kvmem-query-scorer meanq-cosine`).
 Both currently require one GPU, one running request and RAM history; GC with SSD
