 unchanged; target p is constrained and normalized before the existing p/q and residual calculation.
 Existing KV, recurrence replay, token-count, and terminal-prefix commit rules remain authoritative.
 
+### Checkpoint owner budget
+
+All KVMem checkpoint images share the existing `KvmemCheckpointBufferPool` and
+the Program-wide C budget (default 1024 MiB). Each checkpoint carries a move-only
+metadata charge through construction and its final alias; pinned images remain
+charged while live or idle in the pool. MTP's private rewrite rollback image and
+copied metadata use the same account. Required admission consults pool owner
+charges rather than allocating/scanning a directory-based usage estimate. Optional
+LRFU history growth reserves before replacing the snapshot and revokes an
+unaffordable alias instead of publishing stale retrieval state. Metadata charges
+use capacity bounds (including conservative shared attachments), with bounded
+account/control/allocator overhead outside C. This is not an all-process bound.
+
+The existing checkpoint-reclaim path trims idle images and evicts optional older
+owners while retaining the current restore lease. Required quota exhaustion is a
+typed `MemoryError::BudgetExceeded` and follows ordered request-local cleanup;
+optional cache capture may be skipped. The pool caps actual images plus metadata
+charges even for private or unpublished owners that are absent from directories.
+An ephemeral disk read has a fixed reservation inside C and a separate actual
+staging gauge; its worker may finish after cancellation without an early refund.
+
 ### Accepted-source rebuild ownership
 
 The opt-in KVMem source rebuild enters through `Engine::prepare_source_rebuild`, serialized with Engine units. Program reads its own SourceJournalStore, mints a fresh identity with the existing window allocator and prepares an independently charged immutable source copy. Frontend constructs ordinary linear raw-token rows without rendering a chat template again. Program and SourceJournalStore remain exclusive to the immutable model instance; cross-Program/store receipts fail incarnation validation. This is not a tokenizer/model migration mechanism.
